message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Membrane Arena 3x3 + Yin-Yang Shield: a 3x3 lattice of density-matrix cells with an observer and a calibrator (SYNTHETIC classical simulation)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/membrane-arena-3x3"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC classical simulation in Python and NumPy of a 3x3 lattice of
  32-dimensional density-matrix cells with a read-only observer, a bounded
  calibrator, transactional all-or-nothing updates and a circuit breaker.
  "Holographic universe", "Yin", "Yang" and "Schumann" are names only; the
  7.83 Hz signal is an arbitrary sinusoid with no physical claim. Not quantum
  hardware, not a control system. The README documents measured behavior and
  known limits, including that the default settings latch the breaker after
  about 8 steps.
keywords:
  - "synthetic"
  - "density-matrix"
  - "simulation"
  - "fail-closed"
  - "numpy"
  - "python"
